# Intent: The More screen at finger size (owner review 2026-11-18, docs/design/screen-style.md), made together with SF69 (the project name and the affiliation notice on the version page: SF69 alone overflows the page by 42 px, docs/dev/version-page-fit.md). The screen sits under the 28 px status bar with a 56 px header (the title and a 72 by 48 Back or Done target); below it a scrolling column holds the page: every button is 56 px high, the text is the 16 and 20 px Noto fonts (the 14 px Montserrat is gone), the version page scrolls with the affiliation notice as its last row, and a thin scroll bar shows there is more. SF69's strings are unchanged. Display only: no safety, lock, cue, limiter or head-motion code.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_more.cc (ours)
# Check after a flash: More shows a header with the title and Done, then one big button per row (Time zone, Version, Games, Lock, Quick settings) that scrolls; Version shows MaiPai for StackChan, the six detail lines and, after scrolling down, the notice as the last row; Back returns to the menu.
# Kconfig: none

